  MEASUREMENT BACK-ACTION, stated rather than left to be found. The two largest
  excursions (50.11 s / 40.42 s, 04:19:14-04:20:06) sit exactly where I ran
  `cpu-show 0.4` — which `docker exec`s bash into each container THREE times.
  Under a 0.40 CPU quota those exec'd processes draw on the SAME quota as the node,
  so my own read-back briefly stole the loop's budget. The 36.4 s gap at 03:38:03
  appears on ALL FOUR nodes in the same second, which no per-node cause explains;
  it coincides with a host-side `docker compose logs` + `docker stats` sweep.
  These are artifacts of instrumenting the run, not node behaviour — and every one
  of them is still FAR under the 60 s 'does not reproduce' threshold, so nothing in
  the verdict rests on how they are classified.
